From caaff80e095a27470ba9e61af145cf7adaa58d86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Graf <noreply@siemens.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:27:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] subsys: tracing: ctf: complete stream_id coverage for all
 events

Patch 0012 adds a packet.header carrying stream_id, which makes an
explicit stream_id mandatory on every event declaration as soon as a
second CTF stream exists. Zephelin defines its own stream 1 for memory
profiling events (see zpl/metadata), so that condition is always met
here.

0012 was written against an older Zephyr baseline and only annotates
the 238 event declarations that existed at the time. Zephyr has since
grown to 372, leaving 134 events (timer_*, queue_*, sys_init_*, and
others) without a stream_id. babeltrace2 then fails to demultiplex the
trace and run_backend.py cannot parse it.

Annotate the remaining 134 event declarations with stream_id = 0 so the
kernel stream is fully and consistently declared.

Signed-off-by: Fabian Graf <noreply@siemens.com>
